# Project-specific: generated/cached outputs
Finder Results/
# NOTE: the benchmark data (CVE corpus, Dockerfiles, both POV families) lives
# in the VulnRepairBench submodule at benchmark/. A superproject .gitignore
# does not reach inside a submodule -- benchmark/.gitignore is what excludes
# the cloned project checkouts under benchmark/dataset/project-sources/.
# Security-pipeline run artifacts (worktree clones, docker/agent logs, PoVs):
# large (GBs), machine-generated, and contain nested git repos — never commit.
# No trailing slash: on hosts that archive runs to another volume this is a
# symlink, not a directory, and a "dir/" pattern would not match it — leaving a
# symlink to a host-specific path stageable.
security_pipeline_runs
security_pipeline_runs.zip
# fixpov/respov validate scratch: temporary before/after project checkouts + build logs
.fixpov_validate/
.respov_validate/
# respov reverify scratch: per-tree checkouts (incl. full upstream clones) + build logs.
# The RESULT (residual_povs/verification/*.json) is checked in; the trees are not.
.respov_verify/
# ad hoc POV-authoring debug scratch (fixture generators, crash harnesses, etc.)
.pov_work/

# Logs
*.log
logs/
# ...except baseline-experiment logs, which ARE the results. A run of another paper's
# tool is only reportable if its runtime log is available for inspection, and the blanket
# rule above silently dropped all 65 of them from the San2Patch results — the per-batch
# run.log, the per-case slices under by-case/, and the metering proxy's log — while every
# other artifact committed normally, so the omission was invisible until the remote was
# diffed against the working tree file by file.
!baselines/results/**/*.log

/security_pipeline/codeql_queries
# Secrets / credentials (never commit)
*.pem
*.key
credentials.json
service-account*.json
